<p>An Air Canada Express regional jet arriving from Montreal collided with a fire-rescue truck while landing at New York’s LaGuardia Airport shortly before midnight on Sunday, killing the pilot and co-pilot and injuring dozens of others. The CRJ-900, operated by Jazz Aviation, was carrying 72 passengers and four crew members. Reports said the truck had been responding to a separate incident when the collision happened on the runway. Authorities closed LaGuardia for several hours as the National Transportation Safety Board began investigating how the aircraft and emergency vehicle ended up on the same runway. Hospitalization figures varied across reports: some said 41 passengers and two firefighters were taken to hospital, while others said that by later Monday, nine people remained hospitalized after the rest had been released.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/7ITGSnoHoWF4mT2sjtLWNvC3WBKp0YVkAdhauEcH347ere6mhjB1-6TxR3r3aASUjeK5-YK8CIX0HL2cqFGJ3Ea1CmqZk3wmD7DjvqnQQMPfTUyIRFuqdTH-NkkzvzCnE3E5pBbvdu3X2k_Qzgl8liWMKrmT3G0clgJQ2UGEFMDM6yiZlw7d-vJo0gDT-1A4vabvCKuB-Uku' alt='Damaged Air Canada aircraft on the tarmac after the runway collision at LaGuardia Airport.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Safe touchdown, then disaster: BBC reporting on tower audio said the regional jet first landed safely before colliding with the firefighting vehicle on the runway, a reminder that danger can persist even after touchdown.</li><li>Tower audio: Air traffic control recordings captured repeated warnings of “Stop, stop, stop” to the vehicle moments before impact.</li><li>Runway speed: Flightradar24 data cited by The Week said the jet was traveling about 130mph just before it struck the truck, underscoring how little time crews had to react.</li><li>Controller aftermath: In later tower audio, a shaken controller reportedly said, “We were dealing with an emergency earlier and I messed up,” capturing the stress surrounding the response.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>US Transportation Secretary Sean Duffy: Duffy said seat belts helped save lives in the crash aftermath, pointing to the value of basic safety measures even in a severe runway collision. (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c78rdze8zvjo'>BBC News</a>)</li><li>Sarah Lepine: The daughter of surviving flight attendant Solange Tremblay called her mother’s survival after being ejected while strapped into her seat a “total miracle,” and said she suffered multiple leg fractures and would need surgery. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/united-states-canada/article/3347657/flight-attendants-survival-miracle-after-ejection-air-canada-jet'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li><li>WSWS analysis: The outlet argued the collision may have been linked to controller overwork, citing claims that one controller was handling two jobs at the time. (<a href='https://www.wsws.org/en/articles/2026/03/24/wcid-m24.html'>World Socialist Web Site</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/air-canada-plane-crash-new-york-laguardia-airport-2-pilots-antoine-forest-killed-had-just-started-their-careers-11258033#publisher=newsstand'>2 Pilots Killed In Air Canada Flight Crash Had Just Started Their Careers</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/video/032326-the-takeout-with-major-garrett/'>3/23: The Takeout with Major Garrett</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/mar/23/air-canada-plane-collides-with-ground-vehicle-at-new-yorks-laguardia-airport-halting-all-flights'>Two pilots killed after Air Canada jet collision at LaGuardia in New York</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c78rdze8zvjo'>&#x27;Like the plane got cut in half&#x27;: LaGuardia crash that killed two pilots now under investigation</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/23/air-canada-crash-at-laguardia-airport-what-happened-who-were-the-victims'>Air Canada crash at LaGuardia a